  "Cut the walls 0.2 mm oversize in the depth passes, then to size in one last pass: cleaner walls and a more accurate size, especially in hard materials": "",
  "How far below Z0 the pen goes. 0 puts the tip on the paper; a spring-loaded pen holder can go a little lower to press": "",
  "{unit} below Z0": "",
  "Pen up": "",
  "How high the pen lifts between strokes. A small lift saves time; it must clear the paper and anything on it": "",
  "{unit} above Z0": "",
  "Back to 2 mm": "",
  "Repeat": "",
  "How many times the whole drawing is gone over: a darker, more even line from a thin or dry pen. Passes that do not line up exactly make the line a little wider": "",
  "Rest": "",
  "How long the pen rests on the paper after it goes down, before the line starts: for gel pens and markers whose ink needs a moment to flow, and for a spring-loaded holder to settle. It is added to every stroke, so many strokes take longer": "",
  "s after pen down": "",
  "Join gaps": "",
  "When the next stroke starts this close to where the last one ended, the pen stays down and draws a short line across instead of lifting. Saves time with single-line text and dashed lines; the marks it leaves are as long as the gap": "",
  "Fill closed shapes with lines": "",
  "Draws parallel lines across every closed shape, as close together as the pen's line width unless you set it. A shape inside another is left empty": "",
  "Direction of the lines: 0 runs along X, 90 along Y": "",
  "Spacing": "",
  "Distance between the lines. The pen's own line width makes them just touch; more leaves paper showing (a lighter shade)": "",
  "Back to the pen's line width": "",
  "Cross-hatch": "",
  "A second set of lines at right angles: darker and more even": "",
  "Outline": "",
  "Also draw the edge of each shape": "",
  "Open lines are drawn as they are. The lines of the fill are joined into a zigzag.": "",
  "Draws every outline once (an edge two shapes share too). Set Z0 on the surface of the paper.": "",
